course: dictionary
lesson: 7643
title: One word, many meanings: programme
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one. «The programme starts at seven o'clock tonight» means a TV show, not a plan. Look at the words around programme to decide what it means.
explain: In UK English, programme ends in -me when it means a TV or radio show, a plan of activities, or a booklet at a play, concert or match. «A breeding programme saved the black-footed ferret.» Here programme means a plan of activities that helps animals.
explain: Programme can also be a verb, meaning to plan something or to make a machine do something automatically. «The washing machine was programmed to start at six.» Careful: a computer program is always spelled program, even in the UK.
fact: Programme (UK spelling) can mean a TV or radio show, a plan of activities, or a booklet at a play, concert or match.
fact: A training programme or an exercise programme is a plan of activities.
fact: Programme is also a verb: to plan something, or to make a machine do something automatically.
fact: A computer program is spelled program in every country, and in US English all the meanings use program.
fact: Taronga Zoo in Sydney runs breeding programmes for Australian animals like the platypus.
exercise: «The BBC programme Panorama showed a spoof film of spaghetti growing on trees.» What does programme mean here? | A plan of activities | To plan something | *A TV show | A booklet at a concert
exercise: «Serhii Korolev was chief designer of the Soviet space programme.» Which meaning fits best? | To switch a machine off | *A large plan of activities | A TV show | A booklet you read at a concert
exercise: Ravi says, «I will programme the washing machine to start at six.» What does programme mean in this sentence? | A booklet about the show | *To set a machine to do something automatically | To watch a film on TV | A plan for the zoo
test: Which spelling is correct for a computer program in UK English? | proogram | programm | *program | programme
test: «The school programme for sports day starts at nine.» What does programme mean here? | A TV show | To plan something | A booklet with a map | *A plan of activities
exam: Which meaning of programme is used in «She bought a programme at the football match to read the team names»? | To plan something | *A booklet telling you what happens at the match | A computer program | A TV show
